<%# locals: (title:, body:, icon: nil, cta: nil, heading_level: "h2") %>
<%# The one empty state: an optional mark, a real heading, the explanatory
    line, and at most one row of actions. Every admin index that has nothing
    to show renders this, so "nothing here yet" reads the same everywhere.

    `title` becomes a heading element — pass `heading_level` so the page keeps
    a sequential hierarchy (the admin pages all open on an h1, so h2 is the
    default and is right for all of them).

    `icon` is a Phosphor name, drawn quiet: this is the admin, and the mark is
    there to soften an empty page, not to decorate it.

    `cta` is either a { label:, path: } pair for the single primary action, or
    a captured block when a page offers more than one route out — see
    owner/restaurant_tables/index, which offers both "generate" and "add".

    The italic voice comes from `.empty-state` in application.css and now
    reaches only the explanatory line, so the heading needs no `not-italic`. %>
<% heading_tag = %w[h1 h2 h3 h4 h5 h6].include?(heading_level.to_s) ? heading_level.to_s : "h2" %>
<div class="empty-state">
  <% if icon.present? %>
    <%# With an argument this is the rails_icons helper, not the local. %>
    <%= icon icon, class: "mx-auto mb-3 block size-8 text-ox-4" %>
  <% end %>

  <%= content_tag heading_tag, title, class: "list-title" %>
  <p class="measure mx-auto mt-2"><%= body %></p>

  <% if cta.present? %>
    <div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap items-center justify-center gap-2">
      <% if cta.is_a?(Hash) %>
        <%= link_to cta[:label], cta[:path], class: "btn-wine" %>
      <% else %>
        <%= cta %>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  <% end %>
</div>
